  "q1": "Is it safe for my saves?",
  "a1": "Yes. The mod writes <code>dp.sav</code> through a temporary file and keeps 60 backups in <code>UltimateFix\\savebackups</code>, each named by episode, chapter and play time. A damaged save is restored from the newest good copy by itself. Still, back up your save before the first start.",
  "q2": "Which version of the game?",
  "a2": "The Steam version 1.01b of <em>The Director's Cut</em>. Every patch checks the game's bytes first: on another build it switches itself off and says so in <code>ufx.log</code>.",
  "q3": "Can I keep DPfix, ZachFix or DP1 Launcher?",
  "a3": "No, UltimateFIXDP replaces them. Remove DPfix (<code>d3d9.dll</code>, <code>DPfix.ini</code>) and the other fixes first. DXVK is fine and comes in the archive.",
  "q4": "How do I install a translation?",
  "a4": "Make a folder in <code>UltimateFix\\mods\\</code> and put the game files there (<code>fontwide.xpc</code>, <code>mes_all.mes</code>), or the <code>text\\</code> folder of the SWERY Localization Tool. Switch it on in F10 → Mods and restart the game.",
  "q5": "The DualSense does not work",
  "a5": "Turn Steam Input off for the game (Properties → Controller). Then the mod reads the DualSense directly over USB or Bluetooth.",
  "q6": "Something broke. What do I send?",
  "a6": "<code>UltimateFix\\ufx.log</code> and any <code>crash_*.dmp</code> / <code>hang_*.dmp</code>, through GitHub Issues or Telegram. Every feature can be switched off in F10; <code>[Debug] SafeMode=1</code> starts with fewer hooks.",
  "q7": "How do I remove it?",
  "a7": "Delete <code>X3DAudio1_7.dll</code> from the game folder. Nothing else of the game is changed; the 4 GB patch, if you used it, is undone with <code>ufx_laa.exe --undo</code>.",
